### Version

1.46.0

### Steps to reproduce

Reproduction available here:
https://github.com/mrmckeb/tmp-pw-ct

1. Install (see README)
2. Run `pnpm run test-ct`

### Expected behavior

Should render a React component.

### Actual behavior

Fails to render React components unless declared within the `mount` function.

```tsx
import React from "react";
import { test, expect } from "@playwright/experimental-ct-react";

test.use({ viewport: { width: 500, height: 500 } });

test("does work", async ({ mount }) => {
  const component = await mount(<h1>Learn React</h1>);
  await expect(component).toContainText("Learn React");
});

function App() {
  return <h1>Learn React</h1>;
}

test("doesn't work", async ({ mount }) => {
  const component = await mount(<App />);
  await expect(component).toContainText("Learn React");
});
```

### Additional context

We've tested this on 1.45, 1.46 with React 18.3.1 and React 19 RC.

I've confirmed this in a real project as well, and on another system (with another engineer).

